WEBVTT

01:54.027 --> 01:57.602
Th-This...
This is Vearn Palace?

02:04.248 --> 02:06.587
And it was buried
underneath the Field of Death

02:06.620 --> 02:07.889
this whole time?

02:12.565 --> 02:13.634
Popp: Hey, guys!

02:14.402 --> 02:15.437
Oww...

02:16.105 --> 02:17.542
So, where are we?

02:17.576 --> 02:22.886
A big floating palace thing...
or more like a gigantic bird!

02:22.919 --> 02:25.525
And we're
standing on its wing.

02:25.558 --> 02:27.929
I've never seen
anything like it before.

02:27.963 --> 02:29.265
No way...

02:29.298 --> 02:31.203
I really don't think
a human being could

02:31.236 --> 02:32.573
make anything like this.

02:32.606 --> 02:35.110
How can something
this big be airborne?

02:35.144 --> 02:38.383
It's energized by the
Dark King's Magic Power.

02:38.416 --> 02:41.656
The entire palace
must be enchanted.

02:49.707 --> 02:51.777
Crocodine: It's made of
some kind of material

02:51.810 --> 02:53.847
that's neither rock nor metal.

02:53.881 --> 02:57.622
It has to be attuned to
Vearn's frequency, somehow,

02:57.655 --> 03:00.327
that's what's giving
it the ability to fly.

03:00.360 --> 03:02.799
The whole place
is made out of it.

03:04.234 --> 03:05.370
Well, what now?

03:05.403 --> 03:07.340
Do we escape with
a Zoom spell?

03:08.944 --> 03:09.946
Come on!

03:09.980 --> 03:11.315
You think we're
going to just

03:11.348 --> 03:13.152
leave Dai and his
father behind?!

03:13.186 --> 03:14.322
Fine. You're right!

03:14.355 --> 03:16.292
Just put me down.

03:16.326 --> 03:18.029
Hyunckel: I hope
they survived.

03:18.062 --> 03:20.066
That explosion
must have happened

03:20.099 --> 03:22.538
during their fight
against Hadlar.

03:23.741 --> 03:27.148
Nothing else would explain
that kind of blast.

03:27.181 --> 03:28.651
King Vearn was forced.

03:28.684 --> 03:31.356
He would not have revealed
this thing, otherwise-

03:31.389 --> 03:33.192
not with all of us here.

03:33.226 --> 03:35.330
Let's find Dai and Baran!

03:35.364 --> 03:37.434
Maam: If this really
is Vearn Palace,

03:37.467 --> 03:40.340
the entrance they used
must be somewhere nearby.

03:40.374 --> 03:42.645
This place is gigantic...

03:42.678 --> 03:45.317
we should probably
stick together.

03:45.350 --> 03:48.724
Hey, Popp - you saw the whole
thing from above, right?

03:48.757 --> 03:51.864
There must be
something you recognize.

03:51.897 --> 03:54.102
N-No... I don't think I saw...

03:54.135 --> 03:57.407
Anything quite like that...

03:58.009 --> 03:58.710
Everyone!

04:00.815 --> 04:01.883
Take a look.

04:05.390 --> 04:08.130
The explosion must've
happened over there.

04:08.163 --> 04:10.467
All the way at the
head of the bird, huh?

04:10.501 --> 04:13.206
And I see a staircase, too.

04:13.239 --> 04:15.912
Hyunckel: That must be
the palace entrance-

04:15.945 --> 04:18.718
the Dark Citadel Gate.

04:18.751 --> 04:22.559
Then Popp, can your Zoom
spell get all of us over there?

04:22.592 --> 04:24.161
Sure! You know it, Big Guy.

04:24.194 --> 04:28.002
I mean, I haven't been there
before but I can see it, right?

04:28.035 --> 04:30.306
Get in real close, everybody.

04:32.879 --> 04:34.014
Here goes.

04:39.893 --> 04:41.028
Hyunckel: This must be it.

04:41.061 --> 04:44.803
Must be. Now we know that
Dai and Baran are in there.

04:44.837 --> 04:46.071
Let's go!

05:07.582 --> 05:10.287
[gasps]

05:10.321 --> 05:12.625
[fearful trembling]

05:12.659 --> 05:14.328
Heyedra: The survivors
have reached

05:14.362 --> 05:17.234
the palace entrance, sire.

05:17.267 --> 05:20.407
Killvearn: An attempt
to rescue the boy...

05:20.440 --> 05:22.812
What shall we do, King Vearn?

05:22.845 --> 05:26.820
A simple welcome would
hardly suffice, yes?

05:26.853 --> 05:29.793
After all, the Disciples
are guests of honor

05:29.827 --> 05:32.497
in my grand palace.

05:41.415 --> 05:43.186
[concerned chirps]

05:43.219 --> 05:44.990
Hey... Gomechan.

05:45.023 --> 05:46.594
You're hurt pretty badly, Dai.

05:46.627 --> 05:48.196
Try not to move so much.

05:48.229 --> 05:49.431
Dai: Hyunckel...

05:49.464 --> 05:51.737
You're all okay.

05:51.770 --> 05:52.906
That's good.

05:52.939 --> 05:56.747
Baran must've somehow managed
to contain the blast...

05:56.780 --> 05:58.149
Where is he?

06:05.330 --> 06:06.733
What's wrong, you guys?

06:06.766 --> 06:09.939
Did... Did something
happen to...

06:21.395 --> 06:22.765
[gasp]

06:25.871 --> 06:27.440
Dai: How...

06:29.345 --> 06:31.415
How did that happen to him?!

06:31.449 --> 06:32.719
Dai, he...

06:32.752 --> 06:35.724
Well, take a closer
look at all the rubble.

06:50.053 --> 06:54.629
I can't be totally certain
of what happened here,

06:54.662 --> 06:57.034
but I'm confident of one thing.

06:57.067 --> 06:59.973
Baran must have used
all of his Draconic Aura

07:00.006 --> 07:03.647
to shield you from
that massive explosion.

07:04.415 --> 07:06.553
And, now...

07:08.189 --> 07:11.730
[worried breaths]

07:26.593 --> 07:29.197
Dai: Hold on... Just hold on!

07:31.436 --> 07:33.205
Maam! Cast Midheal on him!

07:36.546 --> 07:37.849
Maam, please!

07:37.882 --> 07:39.686
I can't, Dai.

07:39.720 --> 07:41.322
Heal-type spells, they...

07:41.355 --> 07:46.232
they only work on creatures with
life energy still in them...

07:46.265 --> 07:47.769
Your father, he...

07:47.802 --> 07:49.706
Dai: What are
you talking about?

07:49.739 --> 07:52.311
That... That's not possible!

07:52.344 --> 07:54.481
Just cast a Midheal on him!

07:54.516 --> 07:56.820
Baran: That's enough, Dai.

08:02.699 --> 08:05.571
I-Is that you... my son?

08:07.274 --> 08:11.215
I can't... see anymore.

08:11.248 --> 08:12.451
I'm right here.

08:12.484 --> 08:14.890
Tell me - what can I do?

08:14.923 --> 08:18.998
Your friends...
Are they... all safe?

08:19.031 --> 08:22.437
Yeah. They are.
They're all here, too.

08:22.471 --> 08:24.776
You saved everyone.

08:24.809 --> 08:26.345
I see.

08:26.379 --> 08:28.282
That's good to hear.

08:28.315 --> 08:33.827
But Dai, listen... there's
nothing that can be done...

08:35.831 --> 08:38.737
I am too far... beyond help.

08:38.771 --> 08:39.906
[disbelieving gasp]

08:41.475 --> 08:44.014
Baran: At the moment
of detonation...

09:12.539 --> 09:17.715
[roaring]

09:27.434 --> 09:29.404
Baran: I used Doruora and

09:29.438 --> 09:32.177
unleashed all of
my Draconic Aura

09:32.210 --> 09:36.886
to suppress the scale
of the Black Core's blast.

09:37.622 --> 09:40.159
But now I have nothing left.

09:40.193 --> 09:44.301
There isn't a shred of life
energy still in my body.

09:44.334 --> 09:46.973
No healing spell can save me.

09:47.006 --> 09:48.142
You're wrong.

09:48.176 --> 09:49.846
A-A real Dragon Knight...

09:49.879 --> 09:53.052
the true Dragon Knight
is unstoppable.

09:53.085 --> 09:56.526
So no matter what,
you won't die!

09:56.560 --> 09:59.297
You - You can't die!

10:02.572 --> 10:04.576
Baran: It's all right.

10:04.609 --> 10:08.215
You see, I am not the true
Dragon Knight after all.

10:09.819 --> 10:16.633
While I... I had some of the
power... I lacked the heart.

10:16.666 --> 10:19.539
You have that which I did not.

10:19.572 --> 10:22.912
That monster who raised you...

10:22.945 --> 10:27.588
he had a far purer heart...
than I ever did.

10:27.622 --> 10:31.830
You don't need to
weep over losing me.

10:31.863 --> 10:36.272
I know that to you,
he's your real father.

10:36.305 --> 10:37.575
No. You're wrong.

10:37.609 --> 10:39.779
He's my grandfather.

10:39.812 --> 10:44.655
It's not... it's just
not the same thing.

10:44.689 --> 10:46.191
Speak up.

10:46.225 --> 10:50.166
I can barely hear
your voice anymore.

10:52.605 --> 10:53.640
Crocodine: Dai...

10:53.674 --> 10:55.276
This is your last chance.

10:55.309 --> 10:58.850
Call out to your father
with all of your strength.

11:00.554 --> 11:03.460
[crying]

11:03.493 --> 11:07.300
Don't weep... my son...

11:07.333 --> 11:09.906
You be strong...

11:09.939 --> 11:14.414
Be strong... and live.

11:19.692 --> 11:24.100
Dad... Dad, no!

12:14.268 --> 12:15.972
Baran: Do not weep, Dai.

12:16.005 --> 12:20.480
Although my body may perish,
my soul lives on.

12:20.514 --> 12:26.559
I will always be by your side
- in the battle ahead.

12:26.592 --> 12:29.230
But, Dad, I...

12:29.264 --> 12:34.876
Baran: We shall always be
together, never to part again.

12:34.909 --> 12:38.683
So don't give up.
Fight on, my son.

12:38.717 --> 12:42.023
And defeat the
Dark King Vearn.

12:42.659 --> 12:45.130
[weeping]

12:45.163 --> 12:48.168
Now get on your feet.
Stand up, my boy.

12:48.704 --> 12:51.776
Dad, wait!

13:00.961 --> 13:04.869
You're gonna be all right,
Dai. We're all here with you.

13:05.671 --> 13:07.107
Dai [thought]: Dad...

13:07.140 --> 13:10.480
I just felt Dad's
heart enter mine.

13:10.514 --> 13:14.856
I finally know... all the
things he never said...

13:14.889 --> 13:19.464
everything he felt...
I heard it all.

13:35.463 --> 13:37.400
[comforting chirp]

13:38.837 --> 13:42.143
Hey, pal... We should
head back to the base.

13:45.918 --> 13:47.086
I'm sorry.

13:47.120 --> 13:50.126
I know that nothing we
say will ease your loss.

13:50.159 --> 13:52.230
But we're in enemy territory.

13:52.264 --> 13:56.940
You know as well as I do
that we can't stop here.

13:56.973 --> 13:59.177
Whoa, wait - what
are you saying?

13:59.210 --> 14:01.917
Do you really think now's
the time to go charging

14:01.950 --> 14:03.920
off after the Dark King?

14:04.789 --> 14:06.025
Are you serious?!

14:06.058 --> 14:08.697
Show a bit of humanity, here!

14:08.730 --> 14:10.099
I mean, c'mon-

14:10.133 --> 14:13.707
the poor guy just lost his
father right before his eyes...

14:13.740 --> 14:15.978
What can he do in this state?

14:16.011 --> 14:18.984
We need to retreat and
come up with a plan!

14:19.017 --> 14:21.321
You guys? Listen to me!

14:22.691 --> 14:24.094
Hyunckel: Popp...

14:24.127 --> 14:28.469
Losing someone like that can
cut deeper than any sword will.

14:31.075 --> 14:33.278
I know that much for myself.

14:36.485 --> 14:39.291
But consider why Baran
might have done this,

14:39.324 --> 14:41.495
not just the fact
that he's gone.

14:41.530 --> 14:46.071
He sacrificed himself
to make a path for us.

14:46.104 --> 14:48.643
With Hadlar and his Royal
Guard out of the way-

14:48.677 --> 14:53.185
getting to the Dark King's
throne should be easy. Right?

14:53.219 --> 14:57.227
But, if we give them time,
their forces will only regroup.

14:57.260 --> 15:01.569
We have to seize the opportunity
that Baran gave to us, Popp!

15:02.370 --> 15:03.607
Yeah, but still...

15:03.641 --> 15:07.681
If we retreat now, then all of
this will have been for nothing.

15:07.715 --> 15:09.285
There are people out there

15:09.318 --> 15:11.956
that are counting
on us to keep fighting.

15:11.989 --> 15:14.863
I know that Dai's
father would.

15:14.896 --> 15:16.666
Okay, maybe so, it's just...

15:16.700 --> 15:18.001
Dai: Popp.

15:19.137 --> 15:22.544
Dai: Don't worry
about me. I'm fine.

15:23.179 --> 15:24.815
They're right. Let's go.

15:24.848 --> 15:27.253
Hang on - are you
sure about this?

15:27.286 --> 15:30.594
That means you'd be
leaving your father behind.

15:30.627 --> 15:31.662
Dai: It doesn't.

15:33.065 --> 15:34.802
My dad is...

15:34.835 --> 15:36.539
He's right here.

15:36.573 --> 15:37.708
Aw, Dai...

15:37.741 --> 15:43.654
He told me to stop crying -
and to finish this fight.

15:43.687 --> 15:46.024
So we have to move forward.

15:46.057 --> 15:49.331
Otherwise, he'll
yell at me again.

15:49.364 --> 15:51.034
[crying]

15:51.067 --> 15:53.205
All right. You win
this one, Dai.

15:53.238 --> 15:57.515
If you want to fight, then I'm
gonna be right by your side.

15:57.548 --> 16:00.520
So, then - let's finish
this and go home.

16:00.554 --> 16:03.426
Let's go kick that Dark
King's butt, alright?

16:03.459 --> 16:04.595
Yeah!

16:10.707 --> 16:13.346
Killvearn: [menacing chuckle]

16:13.379 --> 16:16.953
Killvearn: I think you've got
that backwards, little Mage.

16:16.986 --> 16:20.594
Killvearn: [laughing]

16:20.627 --> 16:21.996
Both: It's Killvearn!

16:22.030 --> 16:23.733
Both: And Mystvearn, too.

16:23.766 --> 16:25.135
Killvearn: I have a suggestion.

16:25.169 --> 16:29.913
Why don't you try repeating
all that... to his face?

16:29.946 --> 16:31.081
W-What?!

16:31.115 --> 16:33.352
Mystvearn: All hail!

16:35.356 --> 16:39.163
Mystvearn: Vearn, the Dark King,
shall grant an audience.

16:43.640 --> 16:44.742
[gasp]

17:18.209 --> 17:21.348
So, you... So you are...

17:21.381 --> 17:26.258
Indeed, child. I am
the great Dark King Vearn.

17:38.584 --> 17:40.620
[chuckle]

17:40.654 --> 17:42.023
Are you kidding me?

17:42.057 --> 17:44.896
That old geezer's
the Dark King, huh?

17:44.929 --> 17:46.097
What a letdown...

17:46.131 --> 17:48.536
But on the bright side
we can go home early.

17:48.569 --> 17:52.209
Yeah - this shouldn't be
too hard. Right, you guys?

17:54.114 --> 17:56.084
[uneasy laughing]

17:56.819 --> 17:58.188
Popp [thought]:
Oh, come on.

17:58.221 --> 18:00.694
Will somebody say
something here?

18:00.727 --> 18:04.100
Now things are even more
uncomfortable than before!

18:05.804 --> 18:07.006
Killvearn: Well, Popp.

18:07.040 --> 18:08.376
It looks like
everyone else is

18:08.409 --> 18:11.214
a little quicker in
realizing that King Vearn

18:11.248 --> 18:14.788
is far more than
meets the eye.

18:17.995 --> 18:19.865
I expect it's
quite a shock to you

18:19.898 --> 18:22.972
former members of
the Dark Army.

18:23.005 --> 18:26.680
While you may not have ever
interacted with him directly,

18:26.713 --> 18:30.286
I know you still recognize
the overwhelming pressure

18:30.320 --> 18:34.327
of our Dark King's
venerable presence.

18:34.360 --> 18:39.203
His calm demeanor must feel
truly... unsettling, for you.

18:43.714 --> 18:47.353
Oh, yeah? And what makes
you think you're right-

18:47.387 --> 18:49.726
you bargain-bin bad guy?!

18:49.759 --> 18:51.094
Killvearn: It's obvious.

18:51.127 --> 18:53.432
It's the same
expression Hadlar had

18:53.465 --> 18:56.706
when he first laid
eyes upon King Vearn;

18:56.739 --> 18:58.643
utter terror.

19:00.881 --> 19:02.283
Vearn: Killvearn...

19:04.187 --> 19:06.926
You don't need to scare them.

19:06.959 --> 19:11.970
Why do you think I went to the
trouble of revealing myself?

19:12.003 --> 19:13.840
Killvearn: Sorry, sir.

19:13.874 --> 19:16.177
Woo-wee. You made him mad.

19:28.335 --> 19:30.640
Well, you've all
made it this far.

19:30.674 --> 19:32.577
My congratulations.

19:34.280 --> 19:37.521
Vearn: I was certain that by
now you would be defeated.

19:37.555 --> 19:39.825
With Hadlar and
his Royal Guard,

19:39.859 --> 19:44.033
our victory seemed
inevitable, to be honest.

19:44.067 --> 19:49.210
And if he had failed, the Black
Core should have done the trick.

19:49.243 --> 19:53.085
Vearn Palace was supposed
to take to the skies,

19:53.118 --> 19:55.456
but only when
all of our enemies

19:55.489 --> 19:58.830
had been eliminated for good.

19:58.863 --> 20:02.304
Even with Baran helping
you in his final moments,

20:02.337 --> 20:05.376
the fact that you,
the Disciples of Avan,

20:05.409 --> 20:10.320
are standing here is
nothing short of a miracle.

20:10.353 --> 20:12.724
Alright. So what if it is?!

20:12.758 --> 20:16.933
Well, you've earned a reward.
Would you not agree?

20:16.966 --> 20:18.435
A token of some sort,

20:18.469 --> 20:22.143
to commend you for your
miraculous deeds, no?

20:22.176 --> 20:23.279
Reward?

20:23.312 --> 20:25.850
See, I have thought it over.

20:25.884 --> 20:30.425
"What gift could they possible
desire? Now, at the end?"

20:30.459 --> 20:34.668
Nothing - only
my complete demise.

20:36.806 --> 20:37.541
And, yet...

20:37.574 --> 20:39.579
Mystvearn and Killvearn here

20:39.612 --> 20:42.919
are both easily as
strong as Hadlar was,

20:42.952 --> 20:45.523
if not even stronger.

20:45.557 --> 20:47.193
You may find it difficult

20:47.227 --> 20:49.197
to claim your prize
in combat against

20:49.230 --> 20:53.472
the three of us - if that
were to be the case.

20:53.506 --> 20:56.344
Vearn: But I shall
grant you that chance.

20:56.377 --> 20:59.183
These two will not intervene.

20:59.217 --> 21:02.991
You have an opportunity
to defeat me at last.

21:03.025 --> 21:05.429
That is your reward.

21:05.463 --> 21:07.734
Vearn: Exciting, isn't it?

21:07.768 --> 21:10.674
To act without the aid
of my two greatest warriors

21:10.708 --> 21:15.315
is something I haven't done had
the chance to do in centuries.

21:20.259 --> 21:21.595
Popp [thought]: No way...

21:21.629 --> 21:24.233
It has to be
some kind of trick...

21:24.267 --> 21:26.004
He's acting like
he's invincible-

21:26.037 --> 21:30.079
but that's impossible, isn't it?

21:30.112 --> 21:32.116
He's gonna regret this!

21:32.149 --> 21:33.452
Shall we, then?

21:33.485 --> 21:36.091
Surely you won't refuse me?

21:36.125 --> 21:37.661
Well, of course not.

21:37.694 --> 21:40.199
Even if you had
Mystvearn and the Reaper-

21:40.233 --> 21:41.835
we're not gonna back down.

21:41.869 --> 21:45.543
We've come this far and won
every battle along the way.

21:47.179 --> 21:48.516
Vearn: Very well.

21:49.785 --> 21:51.589
Then let us begin.

23:37.801 --> 23:40.740
Narrator: The battle against
the Dark King begins at last,

23:40.773 --> 23:44.848
and even alone, Vearn fights
with a smile on his face.

23:44.882 --> 23:47.988
Overwhelmed by his
Dark Aura and Magic Power,

23:48.021 --> 23:50.560
the Disciples of Avan
are driven back,

23:50.594 --> 23:54.500
but not before Vearn
unleashes his fearsome magic.

23:54.535 --> 23:56.404
Will Dai and his
friends prevail?

23:56.437 --> 23:57.908
Find out on
the next episode of

23:57.941 --> 24:00.647
Dragon Quest:
The Adventure of Dai,

24:00.680 --> 24:02.917
"The God of The Underworld".
